WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.920
Andrew Kincanno:
I think sports really teaches you how important

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.260
it is to work hard, to be successful.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.400
It teaches you also how to develop friendships.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:17.240
When you're involved in a sport with another
individual, you're practicing, and you're

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.939
hurting.

00:00:18.939 --> 00:00:22.119
It's tough out there, and you're doing it
together.

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:28.069
Sports is a great experience in terms of just
developing and creating friendships; a way

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:32.650
of life, in terms of the way you work and
also how you get along with people.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:38.640
Back in the '50s there were not that many
scholarships available; so, when I look at

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.170
what Hillsdale did for me ... The opportunity
to go to a college and play would be really

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:48.690
something great ... probably I was the only
guy in the neighborhood who was fortunate

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.900
enough to do that.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:56.010
I've had a chance to coach with Muddy ... He's
had a lot of success ... and then Bill Mallory.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:03.270
We won the conference championship and went
to the California Bowl that we won.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:09.340
I think as a coach it's probably one of the
best things that you work for.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:15.140
Not everybody is fortunate enough to go to
a bowl game; so, when you finally have a chance

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.090
to go and you're successful, it's a great
experience.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:23.659
I can look back at some of my best friends,
playing and coaching now.

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:25.310
You go through so much.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.619
You lose, and it's tough.

00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:28.970
You win, and it's great.

